From: Anland Hyprland Maintainers <anland@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 10 Aug 2026 07:00:00 +0800
Subject: start: launch bundled DMS automatically

The Anland desktop package provides start-anland-dms. Start it for every
Anland session; the helper waits for Hyprland IPC and Wayland sockets and
then launches DMS with the correct Hyprland environment.

---
--- anland-quilt4.orig/scripts/start-hyprland-anland
+++ anland-quilt4/scripts/start-hyprland-anland
@@ -51,11 +51,10 @@
-# DMS is opt-in.  The dedicated launcher is responsible for its user/runtime
-# isolation and waits for the Wayland socket after Hyprland creates it.
-if [ "${ANLAND_DMS:-0}" = 1 ]; then
-    if command -v start-anland-dms >/dev/null 2>&1; then
-        start-anland-dms >/dev/null 2>&1 &
-        children="$children $!"
-    else
-        echo "start-hyprland-anland: ANLAND_DMS=1 but start-anland-dms is unavailable" >&2
-    fi
+# DMS is supplied by the Anland desktop companion package. Its launcher waits
+# for Hyprland's instance and Wayland sockets, so it is safe to start before
+# the compositor creates them.
+if command -v start-anland-dms >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    start-anland-dms >/dev/null 2>&1 &
+    children="$children $!"
+elif [ "${ANLAND_DMS:-1}" != 0 ]; then
+    echo "start-hyprland-anland: DMS package is unavailable; starting compositor only" >&2
 fi
 
 /usr/bin/start-hyprland --anland "$@" &